":"Olitun acknowledging and appreciating the kindness and efforts of others.","pronunciation":"Dag re jhali baysaw – Chasing shadows / Setting net in water","meaning":"Chasing shadows / Setting net in water to stop the water.","meaning_en":"Chasing shadows / Setting net in water to stop the water.","meaning_bn":"ছায়ার পেছনে ছুটছি / জল আটকাতে  জাল বসানো","meaning_hi":"छाया का पीछा करना / पानी रोकने के लिए जाल लगाना","meaning_or":"ଛାୟା ପଛରେ ଗୋଡ଼ାଇବା /ପାଣି ଅଟକାଇବା ପାଇଁ ଜାଲ ପକାଇବା"}},{"id":"","order":3,"type":"text","markdown":"Dare ge jiwi – Trees are life / Environmental wisdom","textOlChiki":"ᱫᱟᱨᱮ ᱜᱮ ᱡᱤᱣᱤ","textLatin":"Dare ge jiwi – Trees are life / Environmental wisdom","audioUrl":"https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/storage/buckets/audio/files/snd_vocab_idioms_advanced_3/view?project=699495910038e39622c5","meta":{"audioUrl":"https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/storage/buckets/audio/files/snd_vocab_idioms_advanced_3/view?project=699495910038e39622c5","textBengali":"দারে গে জিওয়ি","textHindi":"दारे गे जिवि","textOdia":"ଦାରେ ଗେ ଜିୱି","emotion":"Pride","storyArc":"Dreaming Big","growthValue":"Leadership","characterGoal":"Teach others","imageDirection":"Olitun planting a young green seedling in rich soil, showing care and responsibility for nature.","bodyLanguage":"Standing proud and tall, head high, shoulders back, holding cultural artifacts or projects.","learningMoment":"Olitun celebrating cultural identity, heritage, and personal achievements.","meaning":"Trees are life / Environmental wisdom","meaning_en":"Trees are life / Environmental wisdom","meaning_bn":"গাছই হল প্রাণ/পরিবেশগত জ্ঞান","meaning_hi":"पेड़ ही प्राण है/पर्यावरण ज्ञान हैं","meaning_or":"ଗଛ ହିଁ ପ୍ରାଣ / ପରିବେଶ ଜ୍ଞାନ |","pronunciation":"Dare ge jiwi – Trees are life / Environmental wisdom"}},{"id":"","order":4,"type":"text","markdown":"Goj hor do baku rora – Dead people do not speak","textOlChiki":"ᱜᱚᱡ ᱦᱚᱲ ᱫᱚ ᱵᱟᱹᱠᱩ ᱨᱚᱲᱟ","textLatin":"Goj hor do baku rora – Dead people do not speak","audioUrl":"https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/storage/buckets/audio/files/snd_vocab_idioms_advanced_4/view?project=699495910038e39622c5","meta":{"audioUrl":"https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/storage/buckets/audio/files/snd_vocab_idioms_advanced_4/view?project=699495910038e39622c5","textBengali":"গজ হড় দ বাকু রড়া","textHindi":"गज हड़ द बाकु रड़ा","textOdia":"ଗଜ ହଡ଼ ଦ ବାକୁ ରଡ଼ା","emotion":"Achievement","storyArc":"Exploring Nature","growthValue":"Creativity","characterGoal":"Teach others","imageDirection":"Olitun stands with hands on hips, looking out over the village from a scenic hill, representing leadership.","bodyLanguage":"Cheerful smile, hands raised in a small celebration or showing a finished project.","learningMoment":"Olitun enjoying the reward of dedication, effort, and hard work.","pronunciation":"Goj hor do baku rora – Dead people do not speak","meaning":"Dead people do not speak / Let bygones be bygones","meaning_en":"Dead people do not speak / Let bygones be bygones","meaning_bn":"মৃত মানুষ কথা বলে না/ Let bygones be bygones","meaning_hi":"मरे हुए लोग नहीं बोलते/ जो बीत गया उसे बीत जाने दो","meaning_or":"ମୃତ ଲୋକମାନେ କଥାବାର୍ତ୍ତା କରନ୍ତି ନାହିଁ |"}},{"id":"","order":5,"type":"text","markdown":"Atu hor ge disom hor – Village community is the country''s strength.","textOlChiki":"ᱟᱹᱛᱩ ᱦᱚᱲ ᱜᱮ ᱫᱤᱥᱚᱢ ᱦᱚᱲ।","textLatin":"Atu hor ge disom hor – Village community is the country''s strength.","audioUrl":"https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/storage/buckets/audio/files/snd_vocab_idioms_advanced_5/view?project=699495910038e39622c5","meta":{"audioUrl":"https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/storage/buckets/audio/files/snd_vocab_idioms_advanced_5/view?project=699495910038e39622c5","textBengali":"আতু হড় গে দিসম হড়।","textHindi":"आतु हड़ गे दिसम हड़।","textOdia":"ଆତୁ ହଡ଼ ଗେ ଦିସମ ହଡ଼।","emotion":"Gratitude","storyArc":"Dreaming Big","growthValue":"Problem Solving","characterGoal":"Create something useful","imageDirection":"Olitun gestures toward a village map drawn on a board, explaining a plan to classmates with confidence.","bodyLanguage":"Slightly bowed head, hands held together or offering a token of appreciation, warm smile.","learningMoment":"Olitun acknowledging and appreciating the kindness and efforts of others.","pronunciation":"Atu hor ge disom hor – Village community is the country''s strength.","meaning":"Village community is the country''s strength.","meaning_en":"Village community is the country''s strength.","meaning_bn":"গ্রামের জনগোষ্ঠীই দেশের শক্তি।","meaning_hi":"ग्राम समाज ही देश की ताकत है।","meaning_or":"ଗ୍ରାମ ସମ୍ପ୍ରଦାୟ ହେଉଛି ଦେଶର ଶକ୍ତି |"}},{"id":"","order":6,"type":"text","markdown":"Med khon med dag joro – Weeping bitterly / Deep grief","textOlChiki":"ᱢᱮᱫ ᱠᱷᱚᱱ ᱢᱮᱫᱽ ᱫᱟᱜ ᱡᱚᱨᱚ।","textLatin":"Med khon med dag joro – Weeping bitterly / Deep grief","audioUrl":"https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/storage/buckets/audio/files/snd_vocab_idioms_advanced_6/view?project=699495910038e39622c5","meta":{"audioUrl":"https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/storage/buckets/audio/files/snd_vocab_idioms_advanced_6/view?project=699495910038e39622c5","textBengali":"মেদ খন মেদ দাঃ জর।","textHindi":"मेद खन मेद दाग जर।","textOdia":"ମେଦ ଖନ ମେଦ ଦାଗ ଜର।","emotion":"Pride","storyArc":"Working Together","growthValue":"Leadership","characterGoal":"Solve a problem","imageDirection":"Olitun sits in a circle with friends around a small fire, gesturing warmly while sharing a traditional story.","bodyLanguage":"Standing proud and tall, head high, shoulders back, holding cultural artifacts or projects.","learningMoment":"Olitun celebrating cultural identity, heritage, and personal achievements.","pronunciation":"Med khon med dag joro – Weeping bitterly / Deep grief","meaning":"Weeping bitterly / Deep grief","meaning_en":"Weeping bitterly / Deep grief","meaning_bn":"তিক্তভাবে কাঁদছে/ গভীর দুঃখ","meaning_hi":"फूट-फूट कर रोना/गहरा दुःख","meaning_or":"କାନ୍ଦିବା / ଗଭୀର ଦୁ ief ଖ |"}},{"id":"","order":7,"type":"text","markdown":"Mone barij – Feel sad / Heart-broken","textOlChiki":"ᱢᱚᱱᱮ ᱵᱟᱹᱲᱤᱡ","t